503. Next Greater Element II
Problem

Given a circular integer array nums, return the Next Greater Element (NGE) for every element.

The next greater element is the first greater element to its right.
Since the array is circular, after the last element, continue searching from the beginning.
If no greater element exists, return -1.
Example 1
Input:
nums = [1,2,1]

Output:
[2,-1,2]

Explanation

For 1 → Next Greater = 2
For 2 → No Greater = -1
For last 1 → Circularly next Greater = 2
Example 2
Input:
nums = [1,2,3,4,3]

Output:
[2,3,4,-1,4]
Key Observation

Unlike Next Greater Element I, the array is circular.

After reaching the last index, continue searching from index 0.

Possible approaches:

Brute Force
Better (Double Traversal)
Monotonic Stack (Most Optimal)

Approach 1: Brute Force
Intuition

For every element:

Check the next n-1 elements.
Use modulo (%) to wrap around.
Java
class Solution {

    public int[] nextGreaterElements(int[] nums) {

        int n = nums.length;
        int[] ans = new int[n];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            ans[i] = -1;

            for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {

                int next = (i + j) % n;

                if (nums[next] > nums[i]) {

                    ans[i] = nums[next];
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
}

